# Basal Rate Analysis

The Basal Rate Analysis answers the question "how does my basal rate change
through the day?". It shows the basal rate that your pump delivered at each
hour, and how often your loop changed it.

<Video id="basal-analysis" />

## What it shows

### The key figures

| Figure | What it shows |
|--------|---------------|
| **Avg Rate** | The average basal rate, in units per hour |
| **Total Basal** | The total units delivered in the period |
| **Temp Basals** | The average number of temp basals each day |
| **High / Low** | The number of temp basals above and below the scheduled rate |

A temp basal counts as high when its rate is above the scheduled rate at that
time. It counts as low when its rate is below the scheduled rate. A suspend or
a zero temp basal is not in either count.

### Basal Rate Percentile Chart

This chart is like an AGP for your basal rate. The horizontal axis is the time
of day.

- **The median line** is your most common basal rate at each hour.
- **The shaded bands** show the range of variation, from the 10th to the 90th
  percentile.
- **Wider bands** mean that the delivered rate changed more at that hour.

Where the median falls below your usual rate, your loop often lowers your basal
at that hour. Where it rises, your loop often raises it.

### Average Hourly Basal Delivery

This chart shows the average basal insulin delivered at each hour of the day.
Under the chart, the units are added up for **Morning (6am-12pm)**, **Afternoon
(12pm-6pm)** and **Evening/Night** (6pm to 6am).

### Basal Insights

This card gives the **Basal Rate Range** (the lowest and highest rates), the
**Temp Basal Activity**, the number of **Suspend/Zero Temp Basals**, and the
average **Daily Basal Insulin**.

## How to use it

The report opens on the last 14 days. To see if a pattern is still true now:

1. Look at the **High / Low** figure and the percentile chart for 14 days.
2. At the top of the report, select the date range.
3. Select **7 Days**.
4. Select **Apply Filters**. The report loads again for the last 7 days.
5. Compare the figures with the figures for 14 days.

To see your basal and bolus insulin together, select **Insulin Delivery** to
open the [Insulin Delivery](/docs/reports/insulin-delivery) report.

## Good to know

- **Total Basal** includes the automatic boluses that your loop gave, if it
  gives them.
- **Avg Rate** is the average of the recorded rates. It does not take into
  account how long each rate ran.

<Callout type="warning" title="Talk to your care team first">

  A pattern in your basal rate can show where your settings may need a review.
  Do not change your basal schedule because of this report alone. Discuss
  changes with your diabetes care team.

</Callout>
